The reserved-key condition was logically sufficient but the backend still explored a contradictory map-projection branch. A simpler reachable-state invariant is available: initialize the loop target once before the loop, making the callee’s local map have exactly four fixed keys on every iteration. I’m adopting that semantics-neutral implementation refinement so the invariant can pin the unannotated frame exactly and eliminate the backend’s spurious cell branch without adding a rule.
